Rewrite Medical Markdown Files

This is a simple script that rewrites a messy medical school material that was
directly converted from PDF slides into a `.md` files. The output files are
formatted specifically for use by the pipeline listed in

  https://github.com/medical-uc/knowledge-graph-pipeline

This pipeline defaults to an LLM back-end hosted on

  http://jupyter-02.aml1.id.iosda.org:8888

through vLLM running the model `huatuogpt-o1-72b-4bit`. The Hugging Face path of
the model is `mlx-community/HuatuoGPT-o1-72B-4bit`.

The file `TAG_SCHEMA.txt` specifies all the tags and what each of them contain.

To run it, simply use:

  python3 rewrite_medical_md.py raw_document.md \
    -o rewritten_document.md \
    -v \
    --cache-dir ./artifacts/rewrite_cache

To process multiple documents at once, use the `batch_process.sh` script and put
all the input documents in an `./inputs` directory. This script will create an
`artifacts` directory where all the outputs will go.
